-- title:
--   Normalised node isogeny onto the edge family's node fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, let $\iota : W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to W(k)$ be a ring homomorphism, write $\bar{k} = W(k)/pW(k)$ and let $\bar\jmath$ be $\iota$ followed by reduction. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $\bar{k}$ which is special for $\bar\jmath$ (the zero and one Lie eigenpieces are complementary and invertible), has height $4$ (the kernel of the action of $p$ has degree $p^4$), satisfies $\mathrm{Lie}_0 \subseteq \ker(\mathrm{Lie}\,\varpi)$, and whose Cartier module has complementary graded pieces in degrees $0$ and $1$ (hypothesis `hcΦ`), with an additive map $r_\Phi : \mathbb{Z}_p^2 \to \mathrm{NMod}$ of the associated graded Cartier module data which, for every canonical $L$-map $L$, maps $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ bijectively onto the degree-$0$ $\eta$-piece of $L$. Let $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ be the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(p,1)$ (it does not occur in the conclusion). Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over the edge ring `EdgeFamily.edgeRingCharP p` $\bar{k}$, special and of height $4$ for the structure map coming from $\iota$, equipped with $\gamma : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to$ its Cartier module which is a homogeneous $V$-basis (each $\gamma_i$ lies in the $i$-th graded piece and the tangent matrix has unit determinant) and has structure constants the edge constants `EdgeFamily.edgeRingConstants`. Let $f_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the edge ring to $\bar{k}$ splitting the algebra map and killing $\xi$ and $\eta$ (the node point). Then there are $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and a two-variable power series system $\rho_0$ over $\bar{k}$ such that $\rho_0$ is an $\mathcal{O}_D$-isogeny $\Phi \to X \otimes_{f_0} \bar{k}$ with kernel of degree $p^{4m}$, and there are witnesses that the rigidified datum `Rigidified.mk` $(X \otimes_{f_0} \bar{k}, m, \bar\rho_0)$ has $\bar\rho_0$ an $\mathcal{O}_D$-homomorphism from $\bar\Phi$ to $\bar{X}$ and that both the relevant graded pieces (for $\bar{X}$ and for $\bar\Phi$, taken along the identity of $\bar{k}$) are complementary, together with $a \in \mathbb{N}$, such that for each $i$ the rigidification numerator $r =$ `Rigidified.rigidNum` (namely $r_\Phi$ followed by the $N$-maps induced by base change and by $\bar\rho_0$) satisfies $p^a\, r(e_i) = p^{a+m}\, v_i$, where $v_0$ is the class `nMk` of the base change of $\gamma_0$ along $f_0$, reduction and the identity, paired with $0$, and $v_1$ is `nVarpi` applied to the corresponding class of $\gamma_1$.
--
--   This is the normalisation step in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation: at the node of the edge family, a base-point special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of height $4$ admits an isogeny onto the node fibre whose rigidification carries the standard basis of $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$, up to a common power of $p$, to $(\gamma_0,0)$ and $\varpi(\gamma_1,0)$. It is used in the construction of the Deligne-datum line attached to the edge family with the edge structure constants.
